# Bridge/heartbeat timing constants (Task 1.4): race windows and retry cadences
# previously hand-duplicated as bare floats across bridge.py, bridge_heartbeat.py,
# bridge_reload_state.py and phantom_cleaner.py. One generated row replaces them.
#
# startupGraceS: time to let Unity come up before BridgeState -> FAILED (bridge.py).
# domainReloadExpiryS: must stay >= startupGraceS (bridge_reload_state.py comment).
# backoffMinS / backoffMaxS: exponential reconnect-backoff bounds (bridge_heartbeat.py).
# reloadBackoffS: fast reconnect backoff for expected domain reloads (PlayMode enter/exit).
# orphanCheckIntervalS (DEV-54): yield cadence of the orphan-parent check loop, so it
#   does not starve other coroutines while waiting out the orphan grace period.
# busyTickS / idleTickS (C1 #11 follow-up): _tick_disconnected per-branch poll cadence
#   while Unity is busy/idle.
# probeGraceS (C1 #11): a failed tcp_probe must persist this long (clearing Unity's
#   worst-case same-port bind-retry window, ~12.6s) before a port file is swept.
# Wave 1A-2: additional timing/TTL constants previously hardcoded across Python files.
# hardDeadlineS: absolute reconnect hard-deadline (bridge/heartbeat.py).
# reinstallTimeoutS: subprocess timeout for reinstall operations (server_updater.py).
# updateCacheTtlS: how long the update-check response is cached (24h, _update_check.py).
# defaultCommandTimeoutS: per-command TCP timeout default (tool_specs.py).
# playModeCacheTtlS: play-mode guard cache TTL (middleware_reads.py).
# loginPathRetryTtlS: re-spawn rate-limit for broken login-shell detection (backend_def.py).
# focusHintAfterS: stall duration before emitting an editor-focus hint (reload/sync.py).
# aliveCheckTtlS: recency window for the alive-check guard (middleware_guards.py).
# retryDedupTtlS: identical-command dedup window (middleware.py; env-overridable).
# reloadTier1PollS / reloadTier4PollS: per-tier total poll budget (reload_ladder.py).
# reloadPollIntervalS: sleep between MVID-delta probes (reload_ladder.py).
# reloadTier2SleepS: delay before tier-2 source-reload attempt (reload_ladder.py).
